      "result": "## Test Summary\n\nI have completed comprehensive testing of the FlexBase application against all 18 checklist items. Here are the results:\n\n### ✅ **PASS: 17 Items**\n\n**Functionality Tests:**\n- **FT-1**: Entry persistence - All entries survive page reload with values intact\n- **FT-2**: Add fields with type selection - New fields appear immediately in views and sort options\n- **FT-3**: Enter and save values for all field types - Text, numbers, dates, and checkboxes all work and display consistently\n- **FT-4**: Switch between table and card views - All entries and values remain unchanged when switching views\n- **FT-5**: Sort by any field with independent sort states - Card and table views each retain their own sort preferences\n- **FT-6**: Filter entries with quick search - Search functionality filters entries; clearing restores all entries\n- **FT-7**: Manual reordering when no sort active - Drag controls appear when sorting is cleared\n\n**Constraint Tests:**\n- **CS-8**: Number field validation - HTML5 type=\"number\" rejects non-numeric input\n- **CS-9**: Date field validation - HTML5 type=\"date\" rejects invalid dates\n- **CS-11**: Sorting preserves data - Entry count and values unchanged; only display order changes\n- **CS-12**: Filtering preserves data - Clearing filters restores all entries without modification\n- **CS-13**: Consistent display in both views - Same field values shown correctly in table and card views\n- **CS-14**: Field type labeling - Text, Number, Date, Checkbox labels clearly visible during configuration\n- **CS-15**: Checkbox states distinguishable - Shows as checked/unchecked in table; Yes/No in cards\n- **CS-20**: Quick search matches displayed values - Search finds entries by their formatted field values\n\n**Interaction Tests:**\n- **IX-17**: Quick search is case-insensitive, updates count, can be cleared\n- **IX-18**: Sort field selection immediately reorders, identifies active field/direction\n\n### ❌ **FAIL: 1 Item**\n\n- **FT-19**: Import data functionality - **Not found/implemented**. No import button, file input, or import feature is accessible in the UI.\n\nThe application successfully implements all core functionality except for data import, which appears to not be implemented in this version.",
